    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Wait, what is a -1 workbook?? I've never heard of that in my life. Is that some kind of system error or is it actually a thing in Excel? It feels like the code is just behaving completely randomly. Is there anything else that could cause such a weird, non-obvious error?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"-1\" workbook in VBA refers to the \"Backstage\" or \"Switching Workbook,\" which is the template file used by the Excel Application when you haven't created any other workbook yet. When `ThisWorkbook` is invalid or the code runs in an alternate context, Excel defaults to this hidden internal workbook, and your macro is actually trying to write to a non-existent target sheet or the wrong object. This isn't random; it is a common VBA scoping bug where relative references lose meaning outside a specific file context. The most likely fix is to explicitly set `ActiveWorkbook` at the start of your sub before trying to access \"Recon_Report\".",
      "source": "target",
